  "label": "Concept of artistic rendition",
  "description": "The text 'an artistic rendition of jesus' implies that the image is not a literal or canonical representation, but a creative interpretation. This concept is rooted in art history, where artists have depicted religious figures in various styles (e.g., Renaissance, modernist, abstract, or caricature). Understanding this requires knowledge of art movements, artistic freedom, and how religious imagery is interpreted across cultures and eras.",
